From 21481fa93ed3fecab600633b76fc6f9c057d3d05 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: songliyong <songliyong@contributor>


Date: Tue, 4 Mar 2025 11:39:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] USERSTORY - threadpool for dstore engine

1. Porting percona threadpool.
2. Employ transaction granularity scheduling. For dstore, one transaction
   can not run across workers. so we need to ensure one transaction
   has finished or aborted if we want to schedule it out.
3. threadlocal context adaptation for thread pool.
   One thd can run in different threadpool workers,
   we need to init thread-locals if it has not been initialized.
   And clean it up when worker thread exits.
4. remove some rds related mtr testcases. They rely on some of the features of rds.
   transaction_threadpool_timeout, rds_reserved_connections_func3,
   permission_control_kill_rdsroot1_threadpool, enrich_errlog_for_connection_with_threadpool,
   threadpool_rds_enable_active_threads_check.
   Will be added latter when taurus on dstore have these features.
5. support transaction or statement level scheduling
6. threadpool adds some status to information_schema, fix some related mtr testcases
7. code refactoring, add some comment, global variable naming normalization
8. assign current thread context to cde_session, maybe used in binlog group commit
9.Thread scheduler callbacks for the connection per-thread and one-thread
  scheduler callbacks are no-ops. But for threadpool scheduler, it has
  scheduler callbacks. When admin port connection or localhost socket use per
  thread connection handler, different connection use different connection
  handler. So we can not use Connection_handler_manager::event_functions as
  scheduler callback for all connection.

compared with RDS:
1.the following testcases failed both in RDS and MySQL on dstore, They are related to resource
limit feature, not sutable for threadpool.
main.per_thread_connection_handler, main.partition_locking, main.mem_cnt_common_debug,
main.mem_cnt_sql_keys, main.partition_explicit_prune, main.resource_group_binlog_events,
main.resource_group_bugs, main.resource_group_bugs_debug, main.resource_group_thr_prio_unsupported,
main.resource_group_thr_prio_unsupported_debug, main.thread_cache_size
2. all other testcases passed test with threadpool enabled.
